60,3,1,talk,Servas,,"Candidate A is a catalogue, which @Toshio likes, and uses sequences, which fits our current staffing in modelling and code.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Midori,,"Candidate A seems safe, but it mentions soil samples from different zones. @Benjamin, would that be too risky with the field site issues?","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"Candidate D uses the animal facility, which is in great shape! But @Benjamin said breeding colonies are risky.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Midori, A involves field sites, which are unstable. However, C relies on spectroscopy, which @Kenji noted is currently unreliable.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Midori"",""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Toshio,,Candidate A is a catalogue. My research shows these are the most enduring and successful awards. The field risk is secondary to the output type.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Servas,,Candidate B is out; the glasshouses are full. Candidate C is out; the spectroscopy suite is failing.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Midori,,"That leaves A and D. D requires animal work, which is expensive now and prone to delays. A uses computing, which is free.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Kenji,,But A needs field sites! What if they flood again?,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"While A has field risks, D has breeding colony risks, which are statistically worse. A's reliance on sequencing and computing is a strong hedge.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Toshio,,A is the only choice that aligns with the evidence of long-term delivery and current resource availability.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Servas,,I concur. The availability of code-focused staff makes the Atlas the most viable project.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Midori,,I agree. The free computing and the nature of the project make it the most balanced choice.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Kenji,,I guess A is better than waiting for a broken machine or a full greenhouse! I'm in.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,The logic is sound. A provides the highest probability of completion and utility.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Toshio,,Then we are in agreement.,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
